15 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (A multi-panel process diagram illustrates an automated plant phenotyping workflow. Steps include 3DGS scene reconstruction from video frames, plant extraction using 2D and 3D cues, 3D organ-level segmentation, and trait computation for LAI, leaf count, node count, and height.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing a four-stage plant processing pipeline: Input Seeding extracts plant masks from scene images using detections and segmentations, Lifting performs multi-view geometric lifting, Clustering groups plant data, and Refinement adjusts and exports plant point clouds.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Three side-by-side images compare visual reconstructions of a plant using COLMAP \(Dense\), Instant-NGP, and 3DGS methods. COLMAP's result appears sparse and noisy, Instant-NGP and 3DGS outputs are clearer with higher Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio and Structural Similarity Index values shown. Insets show detail magnification for each method.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Grid of colored point cloud images visualizing lift scores by number of cues \(one, three, five\) and selection range \(all, top 20 percent, top 15 percent, top 10 percent\). Color bar indicates lift scores from blue \(zero\) to red \(one\).) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Line chart titled Precision-Recall Curves comparing four methods: Lift, Lift plus Geometric clustering, Lift plus Geometric clustering plus NN-retain, and Lift plus Geometric clustering plus NN-retain plus CIELAB\(Full\). Precision and recall values are plotted, showing the red diamond line outperforms the others, followed by green triangles, orange squares, and blue circles. Legend provided.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Comparison graphic showing two rows of plant images, each processed using different methods: Correspond Gaussian Splatting, Lifting, Lifting plus Clustering, Lifting plus Clustering plus NN-retain, and Lifting plus Clustering plus NN-retain plus CIELAB \(Full\). Each method\220s output includes a zoomed-in view of a leaf, illustrating differences in detail and visual artifacts among methods.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Figure with three labeled sections showing: \(a\) five original greenhouse photos of green plants on white platforms, \(b\) a single reconstructed scene of several similar plants, and \(c\) isolated, segmented images of five individual plants on a white background.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Comparison of plant reconstruction methods in seven columns labeled a to g, with top row showing colored 3D ground truth point clouds, middle row showing predicted colored 3D point clouds, and bottom row showing green rendered 3D mesh reconstructions; dashed boxes highlight areas for detailed comparison.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Two scatter plots compare computed plant traits to measured values. Left: Computed height versus measured height in centimeters with a linear fit, showing R squared equals zero point nine seven eight five, RMSE equals one point eight eight four two centimeters, and MAPE equals six point four three one six percent. Right: Computed leaf count versus measured leaf count with a linear fit and dashed lines indicating plus or minus one leaf, showing R squared equals zero point eight six one six, RMSE equals zero point six three two five, and MAPE equals six point zero one one nine percent.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Two side-by-side heatmaps show Pearson correlation matrices for six plant traits using a blue-to-red color scale. The left matrix presents correlation coefficients, while the right matrix includes significance markers: asterisks indicate statistical significance at p-values 0.05, 0.01, and 0.001. Strong positive correlations are shown between plant height, leaf count, and node count, with detailed values labeled within each cell.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Four panels show qualitative LCR-GS extraction results beyond the validated setting. In each panel, the left side shows a representative 3DGS greenhouse scene rendering and the right side shows the corresponding extracted plant instances on a light background. Panel \(a\) shows mid-stage greenhouse muskmelon. Panel \(b\) shows later-stage greenhouse muskmelon, where arrows mark representative residual regions or locally incomplete separations. Panels \(c\) and \(d\) show sweet olive and peanut examples, respectively, with arrows marking representative non-target residual regions. The figure illustrates plausible extraction but reduced robustness outside the validated early-vegetative muskmelon setting.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
